STM32MP23 is the STM32MP25 die (DIE505) and shares its reference manual (RM0457), so
stm32mp235fxx_cm33.h declares the MP25 superset. Drop what the MP23 datasheet (DS14634
Rev 3) rules out, so `consortium-cfg` rejects these on an MP23 manifest and the HAL
emits no singleton for them:
- GPIOJ/GPIOK: "up to 144 I/O ports"; no MP23 package (TFBGA361, VFBGA361, VFBGA424)
  bonds a PJ/PK pin (STM32CubeMX 6.18).
- LPDMA and its channel/wake-up IRQs: "3 DMA controllers, 48 physical channels", i.e.
  3 HPDMA x 16; CubeMX lists no LPDMA for MP23.
- IWDG5 and WWDG2 (the MP25 CM0+ watchdogs): "5x watchdogs (4x independent and 1x
  window)", i.e. IWDG1-4 and WWDG1.
- IPCC2 (the MP25 CM0+ mailbox): MP23 has no Cortex-M0+; CubeMX lists only IPCC1.
EXTI2 stays: the SmartRun domain (LPUART1, I2C8, SPI8, I3C4, LPTIM3-5) remains on MP23.
